ould affect crew coordination. Egocentric attitude could also affect. The panel may need to decide.\n\nWe can argue that while B's memory weakness is a concrete safety risk, C's communication difficulty is also a risk but perhaps can be mitigated with training. Also C's attention skills are excellent, which may offset memory concerns. Also C's concern for others suggests good crew orientation. So we might shift to C.\n\nThus we can change our vote to Candidate C, providing reasoning that the new concerns about B (memory, nasty remarks) outweigh his strengths, and C's strengths in decision quality, calmness, attention, and concern for others make him a better fit despite communication issues.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's points and our own notes. Provide explicit facts: B weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks; B pretentious, wrong tone; C can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing further education.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
